        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\u0022risks\u0022:[{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that supply stays short of demand and limits how fast orders turn into revenue\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:3,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022fact\u0022:\u0022latest quarter revenue growth on a year earlier\u0022},\u0022direction\u0022:\u0022falls below\u0022,\u0022level\u0022:\u002236.54%\u0022,\u0022why\u0022:\u0022management called supply the governor of near-term revenue and said the supply environment is less flexible than a year ago, so revenue growth slowing under the recent pace would show demand not being converted\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:3},{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that the one-time tariff benefit that lifted fiscal 2026 profitability does not repeat and margins slip\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:3,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022fact\u0022:\u0022latest quarter gross margin\u0022},\u0022direction\u0022:\u0022falls below\u0022,\u0022level\u0022:\u002265.87%\u0022,\u0022why\u0022:\u0022the CFO cautioned that one-time tariff impacts artificially pulled up profitability this year and will not repeat, so a lower gross margin would show that tailwind fading\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:3},{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that expectations are already high after guidance came in well above consensus, so even a beat is sold\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:2,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022fact\u0022:\u0022latest earnings reaction move per cent\u0022},\u0022direction\u0022:\u0022falls below\u0022,\u0022level\u0022:\u0022-6.32\u0022,\u0022why\u0022:\u0022the last report beat estimates and guided far above analyst forecasts, yet the shares fell after it, so another negative reaction to good results would show the bar has been raised beyond what the stock can clear\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:2},{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that spending on AI infrastructure by hyperscalers and their suppliers slows and orders fall back from the record level of the last two quarters\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:3,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022event\u0022:\u0022Keysight reports fiscal fourth quarter orders below the level of the prior quarter, or says AI infrastructure customers are pausing or cutting test spending\u0022,\u0022kind\u0022:\u0022other\u0022},\u0022why\u0022:\u0022management attributed the surge in orders and the first quarter where wireline revenue exceeded wireless to AI data centre build-outs, and analysts pressed on whether the order level is sustainable, so a lower order level would show that demand is fading\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:3}]}"
